# rsync — real-world examples

## Basic remote copy

```sh
# Archive mode (-a: permissions, times, symlinks), compress in transit (-z), verbose (-v)
rsync -avz host:file1 /dest/
rsync -avz /source host:/dest
```

## Checksum comparison

```sh
# Compare by checksum (-c) instead of mtime+size — useful for validating backups
rsync -avc /source/ /dest/
```

## Trailing-slash semantics (the classic gotcha)

```sh
# No trailing slash: copies the DIRECTORY -> creates /dest/foo
rsync -auv /src/foo /dest

# Trailing slash: copies the CONTENTS of foo -> into /dest/foo
rsync -auv /src/foo/ /dest/foo
```

## Homelab examples

```sh
# Mirror the media library from homelab to mediaserver, show progress,
# delete files at the destination that no longer exist at the source
rsync -avz --delete --progress /srv/media/ david@mediaserver:/srv/media/

# Dry run FIRST when using --delete
rsync -avzn --delete /srv/media/ david@mediaserver:/srv/media/

# Nightly home backup excluding caches
rsync -av --exclude='.cache/' --exclude='*.tmp' /home/david/ /backup/david/

# Over a nonstandard ssh port
rsync -avz -e 'ssh -p 2222' ~/photos/ david@homelab:/srv/photos/

# Resume big transfers (keeps partial files)
rsync -avz --partial --progress mediaserver:/srv/media/movies/big.mkv ~/Downloads/
```

## Flag reference

| Flag | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `-a` | Archive: recurse + preserve perms, times, links, owners |
| `-v` | Verbose |
| `-z` | Compress in transit |
| `-c` | Compare by checksum |
| `-u` | Skip files newer at destination |
| `-n` | Dry run |
| `--delete` | Remove dest files not present at source |
| `--progress` | Per-file transfer progress |
| `--partial` | Keep partial transfers for resume |
| `--exclude=<pat>` | Skip matching files |
| `-e '<cmd>'` | Remote shell command (custom ssh options) |
